      "text": "To find the product of the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the prime factorizations of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\).\n2. Find the GCD by taking the lowest power of all common prime factors.\n3. Find the LCM by taking the highest power of all prime factors.\n4. Calculate the product of the GCD and the LCM.\n\n### Step 1: Prime Factorizations\n\n- The prime factorization of \\(18\\) is:\n  \\[\n  18 = 2 \\times 3^2\n  \\]\n\n- The prime factorization of \\(42\\) is:\n  \\[\n  42 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7\n  \\]\n\n### Step 2: Finding the GCD\n\nThe GCD is found by taking the lowest power of all common prime factors in the factorizations.\n\n- The common primes in \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\).\n- The lowest power of \\(2\\) in both factorizations is \\(2^1 = 2\\).\n- The lowest power of \\(3\\) in both factorizations is \\(3^1 = 3\\).\n\n\\[ \\text{GCD} = 2^1 \\times 3^1 = 2 \\times 3 = 6 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Finding the LCM\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of all prime factors present in the factorizations.\n\n- The prime factorization of \\(18\\) includes \\(2^1\\) and \\(3^2\\).\n- The prime factorization of \\(42\\) includes \\(2^1\\), \\(3^1\\), and \\(7^1\\).\n\nTo find the LCM, the highest power of each prime factor from the factorizations is:\n\n\\[ \\text{LCM} = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 \\]\n\nCalculating this step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n2^1 = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 = 3 \\times 3 = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n7^1 = 7\n\\]\n\nMultiplying these together:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM} = 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 = 18 \\times 7 = 126\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Calculating the Product of the GCD and the LCM\n\nNow, we multiply the GCD and the LCM:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Product} = \\text{GCD} \\times \\text{LCM} = 6 \\times 126\n\\]\n\nCalculating this specifically:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 126 = 6 \\times (120 + 6) = 6 \\times 120 + 6 \\times 6 = 720 + 36 = 756\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\nThe product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{756}\n\\]",
